IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PARTS 6 AND 7, THE PARLIAMENTARY COUNSEL OFFICE AND REGULATIONS (ss 128 to 148).
-- Encoded here: legal professional privilege (s 131), delegation and what a delegate's acts are worth (s 133), revocation of delegations (s 134), protection from liability (s 146), a fee recoverable as a debt (s 147),
-- and the status of regulations and notices (ss 147, 147A). Not encoded, because it is machinery (the office, its staffing, and the regulation-making powers): ss 128 to 130, 132 and 135 to 145; the purposes listed in
-- s 147(1), the conditions in s 147(2) to (5) and the reading rule for references in s 147(1)(f) to (l); s 147A(3) and (4). Each is a row of the coverage table in NOTES.md, inert, reason 2.

§ `Section 131 -- Confidentiality`

DECLARE `Kind of client of the PCO` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister of the Crown`
    `a member of Parliament`
    `a government department`
    `an instrument of the Crown`
    `a judicial officer`
    `a promoter of a local or private Bill`
    `a promoter of a local Bill`
    `a promoter of a private Bill`
    `another person`

-- src:879 | client includes a Minister of the Crown, a member of Parliament, a government department, an instrument of the Crown, a judicial officer, and a promoter of a local or private Bill
-- "client includes a Minister of the Crown, a member of Parliament, a government department, an instrument of the Crown, a judicial officer, and a promoter of a local or private Bill." The list is "includes": another person may also be a client (the Act is silent).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 131(3), definition of client (src:879)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of client of the PCO`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a client of the PCO` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `another person` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Kind of communication` IS ONE OF
    `drafting instructions received by the PCO`
    `a communication between a client and a counsel in the PCO relating to the subject matter of the instructions`
    `drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the PCO`
    `another communication`

-- "confidential communications includes (a) drafting instructions received by the PCO and communications between any client of the PCO and any counsel in the PCO that relate to the subject matter of the instructions; (b) drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the PCO."
-- src:880 | confidential communications includes—
-- src:882 | drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the PCO
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 131(3), definition of confidential communications (src:880-882)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of communication`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a confidential communication` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `another communication` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "counsel includes a person who holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2) and is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation."
-- src:883 | counsel includes a person who holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2) and is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 131(3), definition of counsel (src:883)
GIVEN `the person holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a contractor or secondee is counsel` `the person holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2)` `the person is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation` MEANS
    `the person holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2)` AND `the person is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation`

-- (1) Confidential communications between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel (or between a client and another counsel in the PCO) are subject to legal professional privilege.
-- (2) However, nothing in this section limits or affects the rules and practice of the House of Representatives: where the question is one for the House's rules, this section does not decide it (NOTHING: another authority is expressly preserved).
-- Ruling B (fork F11): outside the House's rules, the privilege is the section's own grant, with its own conditions (a confidential communication between a client and counsel), so a communication that fails them is not given the privilege by this section: JUST FALSE.
-- src:876 | Confidential communications between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel (or between a client of the PCO and another counsel in the PCO) are subject to legal professional privilege.
-- src:877 | However, nothing in this section limits or affects the rules and practice of the House of Representatives.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 131(1) and (2) (src:876-877)
GIVEN `it is a confidential communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or another counsel in the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question arises under the rules and practice of the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` `it is a confidential communication` `it is between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or another counsel in the PCO` `the question arises under the rules and practice of the House of Representatives` MEANS
    IF `the question arises under the rules and practice of the House of Representatives`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is a confidential communication` AND `it is between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or another counsel in the PCO`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 133 -- Delegation of functions, duties, and powers`

-- src:891 | The person to whom any functions, duties, or powers are delegated may perform those functions, or exercise those duties or powers, in the same manner and with the same effect as if they had been conferred on that person directly by this Act and not by delegation.
-- src:892 | Subsection (2) is subject to any general or special directions given or conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
-- (2) The person to whom any functions are delegated may perform them in the same manner and with the same effect as if they had been conferred on that person directly by this Act and not by delegation. (3) Subsection (2) is subject to any general or special directions given
-- or conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(2) and (3) (src:891-892)
GIVEN `the act is done under a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within the directions given and conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegate's act has the same effect as if conferred directly by this Act` `the act is done under a delegation` `the act is within the directions given and conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    `the act is done under a delegation` AND `the act is within the directions given and conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`

-- (4) A person purporting to act under a delegation is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation.
-- src:893 | A person purporting to act under a delegation is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(4) (src:893)
GIVEN `the person purports to act under a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation` `the person purports to act under a delegation` `the contrary is proved` MEANS
    `the person purports to act under a delegation` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- (6) No delegation affects or prevents the exercise of any function, responsibility, duty, or power by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, or affects the responsibility of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel for the actions of any person acting under the delegation.
-- src:897 | No delegation affects or prevents the exercise of any function, responsibility, duty, or power by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, or affects the responsibility of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel for the actions of any person acting under the delegation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(6) (src:897)
GIVEN `a delegation has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation prevents the Chief Parliamentary Counsel from exercising the function or removes the Chief Parliamentary Counsel's responsibility` `a delegation has been made` MEANS FALSE

DECLARE `Recipient of a delegation` IS ONE OF
    `a specified person`
    `persons of a specified class`
    `the holder or holders for the time being of a specified position`
    `the holders for the time being of a specified class of positions`
    `anyone else`

-- (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may, either generally or particularly, delegate in writing to any employee of the PCO any of the functions, duties and powers of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, and must ensure that an appropriate delegation is at all times in place
-- to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel during any absence, incapacity or vacancy. (5) A delegation may be made to a specified person or persons of a specified class, or to the holder or holders for the time being of a specified position or class of positions.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): subsection (5) is a closed list of the persons a delegation may be made to, so anyone else is not given by it (JUST FALSE).
-- src:888 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel—
-- src:889 | may, either generally or particularly, delegate in writing to any employee of the PCO any of the functions, duties, and powers of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, including functions, duties, and powers delegated to the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under any legislation:
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(1)(a) (src:888-889)
GIVEN `the delegation is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is an employee of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may delegate the function, duty or power` `the delegation is in writing` `the delegate is an employee of the PCO` MEANS
    `the delegation is in writing` AND `the delegate is an employee of the PCO`

-- src:888 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel—
-- src:890 | must ensure that an appropriate delegation is at all times in place under this section to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel during any absence or incapacity of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or during any vacancy in the office of Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(1)(b) (src:888) (src:890)
GIVEN `an appropriate delegation is in place at all times to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 133(1)(b)` `an appropriate delegation is in place at all times to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    `an appropriate delegation is in place at all times to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`

-- src:894 | A delegation may be made to—
-- src:896 | the holder or holders for the time being of a specified position, or of a specified class of positions.
-- Rule of 2026-10-29 (replacing fork F11's second limb): section 133(5) says a delegation "may be made to" two kinds of recipient and does not close the list with "only", so anyone else is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 133(5) (src:894-896)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Recipient of a delegation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a delegation may be made to` recipient MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 134 -- Revocation of delegations`

-- src:899 | A delegation under section 133 is revocable at any time in writing.
-- src:898 | 134 Revocation of delegations
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 134(1) (src:898) (src:899)
GIVEN `the revocation is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation is revoked` `the revocation is in writing` MEANS
    `the revocation is in writing`

-- src:900 | A delegation made by a Chief Parliamentary Counsel who has ceased to hold office continues to have effect as if made by the successor in office of that Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 134(2) (src:900)
GIVEN `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel who made it has ceased to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation continues to have effect as if made by the successor in office` `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel who made it has ceased to hold office` MEANS
    `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel who made it has ceased to hold office`

§ `Section 146 -- Protection from liability`

-- src:955 | 146 Protection from liability
-- src:956 | This section applies to the Chief Parliamentary Counsel and every employee of the PCO.
-- src:957 | No proceeding may be brought against any person to whom this section applies for—
-- src:958 | any liability of the PCO; or
-- src:959 | any act done or omitted by the PCO, or by the person, in good faith in the performance or exercise (or intended performance or exercise) of the functions, duties, or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
-- This section applies to the Chief Parliamentary Counsel and every employee of the PCO. No proceeding may be brought against any person to whom it applies for (a) any liability of the PCO; or (b) any act done or omitted by the PCO, or by the person, in good faith
-- in the performance or exercise (or intended performance or exercise) of the functions, duties, or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel. Where the bar does not apply the section says nothing.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 146 (src:955) (src:956-959)
GIVEN `the defendant is the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is for any liability of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is for an act done or omitted in the performance or exercise, or intended performance or exercise, of the functions, duties or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done or omitted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a proceeding may be brought against the person` `the defendant is the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` `the proceeding is for any liability of the PCO` `the proceeding is for an act done or omitted in the performance or exercise, or intended performance or exercise, of the functions, duties or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` `the act was done or omitted in good faith` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO`
       AND (`the proceeding is for any liability of the PCO` OR (`the proceeding is for an act done or omitted in the performance or exercise, or intended performance or exercise, of the functions, duties or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` AND `the act was done or omitted in good faith`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 147 -- Regulations`

-- src:1011 | Any fee, charge, or cost payable to the PCO is recoverable by the PCO in any court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the PCO.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 147(7) (src:1011)
GIVEN `it is a fee, charge or cost payable to the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO may recover it in any court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the PCO` `it is a fee, charge or cost payable to the PCO` MEANS
    `it is a fee, charge or cost payable to the PCO`

-- src:1012 | Regulations made under this section are secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 147(8) (src:1012)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulations made under section 147 are secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1013 | If regulations made under subsection (1)﻿(i) authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice,—
-- src:1014 | a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements); and
-- src:1015 | the regulations must contain a statement to that effect.
-- If regulations made under paragraph (i) authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice, a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation, and the regulations must contain a statement to that effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 147(9) (src:1013-1015)
GIVEN `the regulations authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation, and the regulations must say so` `the regulations authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice` MEANS
    `the regulations authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice`

§ `Section 147A -- Regulations may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation that authorises sub-delegated legislation`

-- src:1019 | This section applies to any secondary legislation that—
-- src:1020 | authorises the making of other secondary legislation (sub-delegated legislation); and
-- src:1021 | is required, by its own empowering legislation, to contain a statement to the effect that the sub-delegated legislation is secondary legislation.
-- src:1022 | A failure to contain that statement does not affect the validity of either the secondary legislation or the sub-delegated legislation.
-- src:1018 | 147A Regulations may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation that authorises sub-delegated legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 147A(1) and (2) (src:1018) (src:1019-1022)
GIVEN `the secondary legislation authorises the making of sub-delegated legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its own empowering legislation requires it to contain a statement that the sub-delegated legislation is secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it fails to contain that statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the failure to contain the statement affects the validity of the secondary legislation or the sub-delegated legislation` `the secondary legislation authorises the making of sub-delegated legislation` `its own empowering legislation requires it to contain a statement that the sub-delegated legislation is secondary legislation` `it fails to contain that statement` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1027 | Regulations made under this section are secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 147A(5) (src:1027)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulations made under section 147A are secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE
